{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774735,"nonce":"5PcqIjR1Ewkvc3PFTaVjubLE7FE=","title":"feat(engine): honor explicit workspace inputs: selection; defer outputs: (loud)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #72 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/workspace-inputs-selection` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-24T11:36:12Z · Merged: 2026-07-24T16:10:54Z\n\n\nPer-need workspace `inputs:` selection, threaded from the authored pipeline spec through the compiled IR into the engine, so a step consumes only the output workspaces of the `needs` it names.\n\n**Before:** the engine's `workspace_inputs()` / `input_signature()` took only `needs` and always inherited every need's output workspace; the authored `inputs:` subset was resolved ad hoc at the scheduler caller and the inline `POST /v1/runs` path dropped it entirely (and didn't compile against `StepDto`).\n\n**After:** consumption is resolved in one place — `consumed(needs, inputs)` — that both `workspace_inputs(needs, inputs: Option\u003c\u0026[StepId]\u003e, output_of)` and `input_signature(needs, inputs, output_of)` route through, so the materialized workspace and the skip-if-unchanged signature are always computed over *exactly* the same set. `None` = inherit-all (back-compat); `Some(subset)` restricts. Both persist paths (trigger `persist_run_from_ir` and inline `POST /v1/runs`) thread the selection.\n\nMotivated by ADR-0007 / ADR-0029 (implicit-by-default workspace inheritance with explicit override) and the 2026-07-24 unimplemented-sweep item 4a (`inputs:` selection was the remaining half; the DB layer, trigger path, and a Postgres rerun-invalidation test already existed on main).\n\n\nThe sibling `outputs:` field (per-PATH output publishing) is parsed + validated in the pipeline spec but **deliberately not consumed** — it is a documented no-op, not a silent narrowing. Restricting a published snapshot to an authored path subset needs CAS **sub-tree addressing** (path-prefix snapshot/materialize), which `scarab-storage-s3` lacks (whole-tree only). Whole-workspace publishing is the shipped behavior. Marked at the output-snapshot site in `scarab-engine/src/scheduler.rs`, at the IR-compile boundary in the server, and recorded in `docs/followups.md` with its build trigger.\n\n\n- **Engine unit tests** (ADR-0017, InMemory, no infra): existing inherit-all/skip-empty cases stay green; added `workspace_inputs_explicit_subset_selects_only_named_needs`, `workspace_inputs_explicit_subset_preserves_order_and_skips_empty`, and `input_signature_reflects_only_selected_inputs` (a change in an *unselected* need does not move the signature; a change in a selected one does).\n- **Feature-acceptance test** (ADR-0017 addendum — executes the feature through the real router + scheduler over testkit fakes): `crates/scarab-server/tests/workspace_inputs.rs::explicit_inputs_scopes_the_materialized_workspace_at_launch`. Diamond `{B,C}-\u003e{D,E}`: D declares `inputs: [b]` and receives only B's output workspace at launch (C excluded); E declares no `inputs:` and receives both. The failure mode (D materializing C's workspace) is FakeExecutor-observable, so **no kind-tier case is needed at land time**.\n\n`cargo check --workspace` clean; the touched engine unit tests + both server suites pass. Postgres-gated tests self-skip without `SCARAB_TEST_DATABASE_URL`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}